=== STEP 1 — DELTA ===
- [NEW] api.sparelabs.com `/v1/global/organizations` auth omission is CONTROLLER-WIDE, not single-route: `/v1/global/organizations/{uuid}` (404 NotFoundError), `/v1/global/organizations/key/{key}` (404), `/v1/global/organizations/{uuid}/mobileApps` (400), `/v1/global/organizations/zones/centroid` (400) all respond with NO Authorization header; only the list route returns the hardcoded 200 `{"data":[]}`.
- [NEW] api.sparelabs.com `/v1/global/*` siblings correctly gated — `/v1/global/users` (401 InvalidTokenError), `/v1/global/settings` (401), `/v1/global/regions` (400 schema-validated), `/v1/global/mobileApps` (401 UnauthorizedError — SECOND auth mechanism, "Invalid access credentials"). Omission is scoped to the organizations controller only.
- [CHANGED] platform.sparelabs.com: index bundle rotated `index-DHUgT6Ph.js` → `index-BIOrSDj1.js` (6.0MB); MFE manifest array CONFIRMED hardcoded (4 fixed vercel.app URLs) — no user input reaches `__MFE_MANIFESTS__`; org-settings hosts (`apiHost`/`routingHost`) flow only into client-side fetch base URLs, no script/DOM sink found in bundle scan.
- [CHANGED] forms.sparelabs.com: `main.71d52314.js` now 7.16MB; bundle exposes `/v1/journeyNotifications/{rebookedRescheduled,rebookedReshaped,rebookingFailed,rebookingPlanned}` POST endpoints (webhook-style push surface).
- [NEW] api.sparelabs.com: OpenAPI spec not exposed at `/openapi.json`, `/swagger.json`, `/v1/openapi.json`, `/api-docs`, `/docs` (all 404) — route map derived from bundle analysis only.

=== STEP 2 — PRIORITIZE ===
- [PRIO] api.sparelabs.com: 7.30 (attack 8, business 8, tech 8, gate 6, cloud 6, fresh 6) — controller-wide unauth now confirmed on 6 routes.
- [PRIO] platform.sparelabs.com: 6.30 (attack 6, business 7, tech 8, gate 5, cloud 6, fresh 5)
